      "thinking": "Let me analyze this certificate markdown.\n\nDocument-level:\n- number: R49/2013-NL1-16.03 (revision 1 annex 1)\n- scheme: This appears to be OIML-CS. The number format \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\" — scheme A or B? OIML-CS certificates under Scheme A are issued by Issuing Authorities of OIML member states... Actually, both schemes involve issuing authorities. Scheme A is for basic conformity, Scheme B for... Hmm. Typically certificates numbered like \"R60/2000-NL1-xx\" are OIML certificates of conformity under the old system, now incorporated into OIML-CS. Scheme A certificates are those based on type evaluation reports (OIML certificates). Scheme B... Actually in OIML-CS, Scheme A = OIML certificate (with OIML type evaluation), Scheme B = national certificates. Given this is issued by NMi as OIML Issuing Authority NL1, it's Scheme A. The instruction: scheme (A|B). I'll use \"A\" since it's an OIML Issuing Authority certificate. Hmm, but is there evidence? The header says \"OIML CS — Certification System\" logo. NMi Certin B.V., OIML Issuing Authority NL1. This is a classic OIML certificate (Scheme A). I'll say \"A\".\n\n- project_number: 16200309\n- page_total: 1\n- member_state: Netherlands\n- date_issued: 2018-03-22 (22 March 2018)\n- oiml_issuer_id: NL1\n\nIssuing authority:\n- name: NMi Certin B.V.\n- address_lines: [\"Hugo de Grootplein 1\", \"3314 EG Dordrecht\", \"the Netherlands\"]\n- person_responsible: C. Oosterman\n- person_title: Head Certification Board\n- phone: +31 78 6332332\n- email: certin@nmi.nl\n- website: www.nmi.nl\n- oiml_issuer_id: NL1\n\nApplicants[]:\n- name: Euromag International S.r.l.\n- address_lines: [\"Via della Tecnica 20\", \"35035 Mestrino (PD)\", \"Italy\"]\n\nManufacturers[]: same as applicant (Applicant and Manufacturer row).\n\nCertified type:\n- category: \"Water meter\" (electromagnetic water meter) — the schema examples say \"Gas meter\", so \"Water meter\".\n- type_designations: MUT2300, MUT2200EL, MC406M (electronic converter). The type is \"MUT2300 and MUT2200EL with electronic converter MC406M\". So type_designations: [\"MUT2300\", \"MUT2200EL\", \"MC406M\"]. Actually MC406M is a converter component — could be components. The text: \"Type : MUT2300 and MUT2200EL with electronic converter MC406M\". I'd list type_designations: [\"MUT2300\", \"MUT2200EL\"] and components: [{role: \"electronic converter\", type_designations: [\"MC406M\"]}]. Or include MC406M in type_designations. Both defensible. I'll do type_designations: [\"MUT2300\", \"MUT2200EL\", \"MC406M\"] and also components entry for MC406M as electronic converter. Hmm, maybe better: type_designations: [\"MUT2300\", \"MUT2200EL\"], components: [{role: \"electronic converter\", type_designations: [\"MC406M\"]}]. But rule says type_designations[] = all type/model identifiers mentioned. I'll include all three in type_designations and also component.\n\n- module_designation: null (not applicable — water meters... could be \"Not applicable\"? Not stated; omit or null).\n- description: \"An electromagnetic water meter\" / \"An electromagnetic water meter, Type MUT2300 and MUT2200EL with electronic converter MC406M\"\n\nModel family: two model variants MUT2300 and MUT2200EL. Include models: [{model_id: \"MUT2300\"}, {model_id: \"MUT2200EL\"}]. Family name null.\n\nRecommendation: R49 — but edition? Not stated. The number R49/2013-NL1-16.03 suggests recommendation R49, edition 2013. The number format is \"R{edition}/{...}\"? Actually NMi format: \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\" — typically NMi OIML certificate numbers are like \"R60/2000-NL1-2009-02\" where 2013 could be the year of first issue... Hmm. Format examples: \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\". NMi certificate numbering: recommendation/year-NL1-number. E.g., \"R137/2013-NL1-16.05\" — here 2013 could be the edition year of R49? R49 editions: 2013 (R49-1:2013). Yes! OIML R49 was published in 2013 edition (CD? Actually R49-1:2013 exists). Hmm, R49 \"Water meters intended for the metering of cold potable water and hot water\" — parts 1-3 published 2013. Yes, R49-1/-2/-3 edition 2013. And the numbering scheme for NMi is \"R{rec}/{year}-NL1-{YY}.{seq}\" where year likely the edition. E.g., \"R60/2000-NL1-2009-03\" for R60 edition 2000. So \"R49/2013\" implies edition 2013.\n\nBut rule 8 says don't fabricate. The edition isn't explicitly stated. However the canonical id \"R49\" is extractable from the number. I think including recommendation: {id: \"R49\", edition: 2013} is a reasonable inference... but risky. The format \"R49/2013\" strongly parallels \"R60/2000\" where 2000 is the R60 edition. Given OIML R49-1/-2/-3 are dated 2013, I'll include edition 2013. Actually, is there any R49 edition 2013? OIML R49-1:2013 \"Water meters intended for the metering of cold potable water and hot water — Part 1: Metrological and technical requirements\" — yes, published 2013. I'll include edition: 2013.\n\nScheme for recommendation: The recommendation schema has \"scheme\" field? Looking at schema: recommendation: {id, edition, amendment, scheme, accuracy_classes[]}. Hmm, scheme in recommendation? Maybe refers to which scheme (A/B) applies. I'll omit since not stated. accuracy_classes: not stated, omit.\n\nTest reports:\n- Type Evaluation Report NMi–16200309–01 revision 1. role: type_evaluation_report. id: \"NMi-16200309-01\". date: not given. pages: not given.\n\nRevision history:\n- Number says \"revision 1 annex 1\". Correction row: \"The Type Evaluation Report NMi–16200309–01 revision 1 is made due to the missing test data in the Annex 2 of the MUT2200EL size DN200.\"\n- revision_history: [{revision: \"1\", date: null, changes: \"The Type Evaluation Report NMi–16200309–01 revision 1 is made due to the missing test data in the Annex 2 of the MUT2200EL size DN200.\"}]\n\nHmm — the revision 1 refers to the annex/certificate? \"Number R49/2013-NL1-16.03 revision 1 annex 1\". So the certificate number is revision 1, annex 1. The correction note mentions the TER revision 1.\n\nI could include revision_history entry with revision \"1\" and changes about the TER revision due to missing test data. That seems the best interpretation.\n\nFootnotes: none.\n\nCharacteristics: Not much numeric. MUT2200EL size DN200 mentioned — DN200 is a size. Could add config_level or model_level? There's mention of \"Annex 2 of the MUT2200EL size DN200\" — MUT2200EL comes in sizes including DN200. Could model the DN200 as a variant? We only know one size. I could add a model-level attribute \"nominal_size\" for MUT2200EL: DN200? That's only evidence that DN200 exists; the model might have multiple sizes. Rule 8: don't fabricate. I might add attributes: type_level none. Maybe add a characteristic \"nominal_size_dn\" with model_level? Hmm, \"MUT2200EL size DN200\" indicates a variant. I could add model \"MUT2200EL DN200\"? That may overreach. I'll keep it simple: models MUT2300 and MUT2200EL. Maybe note DN200 in description or matrix? I'll skip.\n\nCertificate number: should include revision/annex? number: \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\". Maybe number \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\" and note revision 1 annex 1 — there's no field for annex. I could put number: \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03 revision 1 annex 1\"? Better keep clean: number: \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\". Hmm, the revision_history covers revision 1.\n\ndate_issued: \"2018-03-22\". Format? Schema doesn't specify; ISO is fine.\n\nCategory: \"Water meter\". The schema example includes \"Gas meter\" so \"Water meter\" fits.\n\nmodel_family: include only if cert covers >1 model variant. Here two types: MUT2300 and MUT2200EL. So include with models both. family_name: null.\n\nAlso MC406M converter as component.\n\nFinal JSON:\n\n{\n  \"certificate\": {\n    \"number\": \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\",\n    \"scheme\": \"A\",\n    \"project_number\": \"16200309\",\n    \"page_total\": 1,\n    \"member_state\": \"Netherlands\",\n    \"date_issued\": \"2018-03-22\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"issuing_authority\": {\n    \"name\": \"NMi Certin B.V.\",\n    \"address_lines\": [\"Hugo de Grootplein 1\", \"3314 EG Dordrecht\", \"the Netherlands\"],\n    \"person_responsible\": \"C. Oosterman\",\n    \"person_title\": \"Head Certification Board\",\n    \"phone\": \"+31 78 6332332\",\n    \"email\": \"certin@nmi.nl\",\n    \"website\": \"www.nmi.nl\",\n    \"oiml_issuer_id\": \"NL1\"\n  },\n  \"applicants\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Euromag International S.r.l.\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Via della Tecnica 20\", \"35035 Mestrino (PD)\", \"Italy\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"manufacturers\": [\n    {\n      \"name\": \"Euromag International S.r.l.\",\n      \"address_lines\": [\"Via della Tecnica 20\", \"35035 Mestrino (PD)\", \"Italy\"]\n    }\n  ],\n  \"certified_type\": {\n    \"category\": \"Water meter\",\n    \"type_designations\": [\"MUT2300\", \"MUT2200EL\", \"MC406M\"],\n    \"module_designation\": null,\n    \"description\": \"An electromagnetic water meter, types MUT2300 and MUT2200EL with electronic converter MC406M\"\n  },\n  \"model_family\": {\n    \"family_name\": null,\n    \"models\": [\n      {\"model_id\": \"MUT2300\", \"label\": \"MUT2300\", \"attributes\": {}},\n      {\"model_id\": \"MUT2200EL\", \"label\": \"MUT2200EL\", \"attributes\": {}}\n    ]\n  },\n  \"components\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"electronic converter\",\n      \"type_designations\": [\"MC406M\"],\n      \"alternatives\": null,\n      \"characteristics\": {}\n    }\n  ],\n  \"recommendation\": {\n    \"id\": \"R49\",\n    \"edition\": 2013\n  },\n  \"test_reports\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"NMi-16200309-01\",\n      \"role\": \"type_evaluation_report\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_history\": [\n    {\n      \"revision\": \"1\",\n      \"date\": null,\n      \"changes\": \"The Type Evaluation Report NMi–16200309–01 revision 1 is made due to the missing test data in the Annex 2 of the MUT2200EL size DN200.\"\n    }\n  ]\n}\n\nWait — the revision history: revision \"1\" of the certificate annex. The changes text describes TER revision. It's fine.\n\nShould scheme be \"A\"? Let me reconsider. OIML-CS: Scheme A issues OIML Certificates of Conformity based on evaluation by issuing authorities; Scheme B certificates issued by member states' national services. NMi as \"OIML Issuing Authority NL1\" issues under Scheme A (the classic OIML certificate system). The logo \"OIML CS\" confirms OIML Certification System. I'll use \"A\".\n\nAlso consider certificate.number: include \"annex 1\"? I'll keep \"R49/2013-NL1-16.03\" clean.\n\nThe en-dash in \"NMi–16200309–01\" — normalize to \"NMi-16200309-01\".\n\nI'll include oiml_issuer_id at certificate level: \"NL1\".\n\nPage total: \"Page 1 of 1\" → 1.\n\nDone.",
